# Definition of Done

> The registry currently pushes this check onto each tool's own executor, leaving every consumer to implement it itself — differently each time, or not at all.

**Strategy: `direct`** — `ToolRegistry.execute` is an existing callable seam, so the acceptance tests exercise the registry and the real orchestrator path directly.

## Done when these pass

- [ ] **rejects invalid input without exposing values and preserves valid input** — rejected required and wrong-typed fields return a useful tool result, do not call the executor, and do not expose the supplied value in logs or result text; valid extra properties arrive unchanged.
      `src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts`
- [ ] **rejects an invalid schema when registering its tool** — broken static schemas fail at registration with the tool name; unknown names retain their existing throw.
      `src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts`
- [ ] **validates function sourced tools against the current schema** — each function-valued definition's current schema controls validation.
      `src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts`
- [ ] **returns a rejected call to the provider so it can correct the input next round** — the actual tool loop completes and exposes the rejection to the next provider round.
      `src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts`

## Facets

- [ ] Return validation failures as `ToolResponse` values before invoking the executor.
- [ ] Preserve valid input, extra properties, and the unknown-tool exception behavior.
- [ ] Compile invalid static schemas at registration and resolve function-valued definitions per call.
- [ ] Feed a validation rejection through the tool loop for a later model retry.

## Out of scope

- Tool output validation, authorization, retries beyond the existing tool-round limit, and edits to tool implementations or user-facing documentation.
# Tool Input Validation

| Field  | Value                |
| ------ | -------------------- |
| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
| Status | Draft                |

The tool registry validates a call against the registered tool's JSON Schema before an executor can observe it.

## Contract

- `ToolRegistry.execute` checks an input against the resolved tool definition's `inputSchema` before invoking the executor; rejected input returns a `ToolResponse` describing the invalid field and does not invoke the executor ([validated by: rejects invalid input without exposing values and preserves valid input](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L18)).
- Valid input, including undeclared extra properties, reaches the executor unchanged and exactly once ([validated by: rejects invalid input without exposing values and preserves valid input](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L18)).
- An invalid schema fails during static tool registration with an error naming the tool ([validated by: rejects an invalid schema when registering its tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L58)).
- A function-valued definition is resolved for each execution, and its current schema governs that call ([validated by: validates function sourced tools against the current schema](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L70)).
- A rejected tool call is returned to the provider as a tool result so a later round can correct the input ([validated by: returns a rejected call to the provider so it can correct the input next round](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L98)).
import {jest} from '@jest/globals';
import {ToolRegistry} from './registry.js';
import {createChatOrchestrator} from '../chatOrchestrator.js';
import {PromptBuilder} from '../../infrastructure/builders/promptBuilder.js';
import type {AIProvider, MessageChunk, SendMessageParams} from '../../types/ai.js';

const requiredLocation = {
  name: 'weather',
  description: 'Looks up the weather',
  inputSchema: {
    type: 'object',
    properties: {location: {type: 'string'}},
    required: ['location'],
  },
};

describe('ToolRegistry input schema acceptance', () => {
  it('rejects invalid input without exposing values and preserves valid input', async () => {
    const registry = new ToolRegistry();
    let calls = 0;
    const received: Record<string, unknown>[] = [];
    const logLines: string[] = [];
    const logSpy = jest.spyOn(console, 'log').mockImplementation((line: unknown) => logLines.push(String(line)));
    registry.register(requiredLocation, async input => {
      calls += 1;
      received.push(input);
      return 'forecast';
    });

    try {
      const validInput = {location: 'Berlin', trace: {requestId: 'r-7'}};
      const valid = await registry.execute('weather', validInput);
      const missing = await registry.execute('weather', {});
      const identifyingValue = 'person@example.test';
      const mistyped = await registry.execute('weather', {location: 42, email: identifyingValue});

      expect({
        valid,
        received,
        requiredRejected: /location.*required/i.test(missing.result),
        mistypedRejected: /location.*string/i.test(mistyped.result),
        identifyingValueHidden:
          !mistyped.result.includes(identifyingValue) && !logLines.join('\n').includes(identifyingValue),
        calls,
      }).toEqual({
        valid: {result: 'forecast'},
        received: [validInput],
        requiredRejected: true,
        mistypedRejected: true,
        identifyingValueHidden: true,
        calls: 1,
      });
    } finally {
      logSpy.mockRestore();
    }
  });

  it('rejects an invalid schema when registering its tool', () => {
    const registry = new ToolRegistry();

    expect(() =>
      registry.register(
        {name: 'broken-weather', description: 'Broken schema', inputSchema: {type: 'not-a-json-schema-type'}},
        async () => 'unreachable'
      )
    ).toThrow(/broken-weather/i);
    return expect(registry.execute('missing', {})).rejects.toThrow('Unknown tool: missing');
  });

  it('validates function sourced tools against the current schema', async () => {
    const registry = new ToolRegistry();
    let resolutions = 0;
    let calls = 0;
    registry.register(
      () => {
        resolutions += 1;
        const field = resolutions === 1 ? 'first' : 'second';
        return {
          name: 'changing',
          description: 'Changes schema per resolution',
          inputSchema: {type: 'object', properties: {[field]: {type: 'string'}}, required: [field]},
        };
      },
      async () => {
        calls += 1;
        return 'accepted';
      }
    );

    const currentSchemaInput = await registry.execute('changing', {second: 'current'});
    const staleSchemaInput = await registry.execute('changing', {first: 'stale'});

    expect(currentSchemaInput).toEqual({result: 'accepted'});
    expect(staleSchemaInput.result).toMatch(/second.*required/i);
    expect(calls).toBe(1);
  });

  it('returns a rejected call to the provider so it can correct the input next round', async () => {
    let round = 0;
    let retryContent = '';
    const provider: AIProvider = {
      async *sendMessage(params: SendMessageParams): AsyncGenerator<MessageChunk> {
        if (round++ === 0) {
          yield {type: 'tool_use', toolCall: {id: 'weather-1', name: 'weather', input: {}}};
          yield {type: 'stop', stopReason: 'tool_use'};
          return;
        }
        const lastMessage = params.messages.at(-1);
        if (lastMessage?.role === 'user' && Array.isArray(lastMessage.content)) {
          retryContent = JSON.stringify(lastMessage.content);
        }
        yield {type: 'text', text: 'corrected'};
        yield {type: 'stop', stopReason: 'end_turn'};
      },
      async generateStructured<T>(): Promise<T> {
        return {} as T;
      },
    };
    const registry = new ToolRegistry();
    let executorCalls = 0;
    registry.register(requiredLocation, async () => {
      executorCalls += 1;
      return 'forecast';
    });
    const orchestrator = createChatOrchestrator(provider, new PromptBuilder({identity: 'test'}), registry);

    await expect(
      orchestrator.processMessage({
        sessionId: 'validation-retry',
        userId: 'user-1',
        entries: [{role: 'user', content: 'weather?', timestamp: '2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z'}],
      })
    ).resolves.toBe('corrected');
    expect(retryContent).toMatch(/location.*required/i);
    expect(executorCalls).toBe(0);
  });
});
